			<!-- GPL-2.0-only tree (pascal/kext/README.md). The match dictionary is the
			     same wide net kexts/NVRM/Info.plist uses on purpose: IOPCIPrimaryMatch
			     compares the 32-bit (device<<16 | vendor) word, and its "value&mask"
			     form masks it first, so 0x000010de&0x0000ffff reads as "vendor 0x10DE,
			     any device". IOPCIClassMatch is ANDed with it and pins the PCI base
			     class to 0x03 (display) while leaving the subclass free, so both VGA
			     (0x00) and 3D-controller (0x02) Pascal cards match. The REAL gate is
			     software: PG106::probe() (src/PG106.cpp) accepts only the GP10x Helios
			     300 ids in src/pg106_device_gate.c (1C20/1C23/1C60 GP106M etc.,
		     HELIOS300-PASCAL-RESEARCH.md §1). Never narrow this match to one id. -->
			<key>IOPCIPrimaryMatch</key>
			<string>0x000010de&amp;0x0000ffff</string>
			<key>IOPCIClassMatch</key>
			<string>0x03000000&amp;0xff000000</string>
			<key>IOProbeScore</key>
			<integer>1000</integer>
		</dict>
